From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: skip binding flows destined to the local host

The PPE driver binds flows seen on the wire even when they are addressed
to the router itself (destination MAC equals a local interface address,
i.e. traffic to the router's own IP). Such flows must be delivered to
the CPU and must never be offloaded to the hardware: committing a local
flow produces a broken PPE entry (observed with the ethertype cleared)
that drops traffic after the first burst, limiting local throughput to
~128KB/256K on the 10G LAN port when flow_offloading_hw is enabled.

Skip the hardware bind for packets whose destination MAC matches the
ingress device or its bridge master.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1689,6 +1689,31 @@ int airoha_ppe_setup_tc_block_cb(struct airoha_ppe_dev *dev, void *type_data)
 	return err;
 }
 
+static bool airoha_ppe_skb_is_local(struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	const u8 *dest = eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest;
+	struct net_device *dev = skb->dev;
+	struct net_device *master;
+
+	if (!dev)
+		return false;
+
+	if (ether_addr_equal(dest, dev->dev_addr))
+		return true;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	master = airoha_ppe_foe_get_bridge_master_rcu(dev);
+	if (master) {
+		bool local = ether_addr_equal(dest, master->dev_addr);
+
+		rcu_read_unlock();
+		return local;
+	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 void airoha_ppe_check_skb(struct airoha_ppe_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
 			  u16 hash, bool rx_wlan)
 {
@@ -1699,6 +1724,15 @@ void airoha_ppe_check_skb(struct airoha_ppe_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
 	if (hash > ppe_hash_mask)
 		return;
 
+	/* Flows addressed to the router itself must be delivered to the CPU
+	 * and must never be offloaded to the PPE. Committing a local flow
+	 * produces a broken PPE entry that drops traffic after the first
+	 * burst (128KB throughput cliff on the 10G LAN port observed with
+	 * flow_offloading_hw enabled).
+	 */
+	if (airoha_ppe_skb_is_local(skb))
+		return;
+
 	now = (u16)jiffies;
 	diff = now - ppe->foe_check_time[hash];
 	if (diff < HZ / 10)
